<TextPage
	title="About — Hookd"
	description="A personal crochet blog: free patterns written out in full, and write-ups of yarn, fibre and stitch tests. Not a shop."
	heading="About"
	standfirst="Free crochet patterns, and write-ups of the tests behind them."
	active="about"
>
	<p>
		I design crochet patterns and test the yarn that goes into them. The testing happened
		privately for years — swatches, wash tests, gauge measured twice and written on a scrap of
		paper that went in a drawer. This site is where that stops being private.
	</p>

	<h2>What is here</h2>

	<p>
		<strong>Free patterns</strong>, written out in full. No video-only instructions, no
		paywall, no partial pattern with the good part behind a purchase. Sizes and gauge are
		stated the way the Craft Yarn Council defines them, and every pattern carries both a swatch
		gauge and a piece gauge — because those two numbers differ, and almost no published pattern
		admits it.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>The journal</strong> is the working-out: yarn tests, stitch tests, fibre notes.
		Everything gets swatched, washed and measured before it gets written about, including the
		results that were inconvenient.
	</p>

	<h2>What is not here</h2>

	<p>
		This is not a shop and it will not become one. There are no carts, no accounts, no
		newsletter pop-up over the recipe. Anything I sell lives on Ravelry, never here.
	</p>

	<p>
		The patterns published here stay free. Not as an introductory offer — free.
	</p>

	<h2>Using the patterns</h2>

	<p>
		Make them, gift them, and sell what you make. The <a href="/licence/">pattern terms</a> set
		that out properly, but that is the short version.
	</p>

